WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.324 --> 00:00:02.822
(intense music)

00:00:02.822 --> 00:00:04.905
(typing)

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:10.980
- People who are not in STEM
kind of have an outside look

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:12.380
at software development,

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:15.800
sometimes don't understand
how truly creative it is.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:18.220
Reading lines of code
is like reading poetry.

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:21.120
It's an art form in
itself, and it's a culture

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.529
of really bringing ideas to light.

00:00:24.529 --> 00:00:27.362
(slow jazz music)

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.640
I started coding when I was 9 years old,

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:37.853
and I've been dancing since,
I think, I was able to walk.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.750
My father is a dancer,
so it was in my blood.

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:44.620
So, there's one where
Mateo is on his own...

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:47.300
So, I had a plan in
life, I had a direction.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.670
I was going to be a professional dancer.

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:53.340
Everything was lined up
and then I got cancer.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:56.453
It changed the whole path of my life.

00:00:57.380 --> 00:00:59.020
While I was in recovery,

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:00.610
I'm not really good at sitting still,

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:03.160
so I was writing software
from a hospital bed.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:04.730
I'd gotten almost obsessed, like,

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:06.240
it was something that just kept me going.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:10.793
And when I came back home,
I wanted to dance again.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:13.330
I was in the midst of trying to find ways

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:14.650
to mix dance and technology.

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:17.940
And that's when I came up with
the idea of the light suits

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:19.950
and wirelessly programming them to make

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:21.933
really amazing visual art.

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:25.972
Alright, I'm going to stop
at this queue when it starts.

00:01:25.972 --> 00:01:26.890
(pulsing easy techno music)

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:29.560
Let's just see if this is
right before they dance.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:32.900
We we're up hours and hours
and hours writing this software

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:35.020
and trying different things.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:36.800
And it was just a lot of fun.

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:38.350
The end product is as simple as me

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:40.160
pressing one button and the lights turn on

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:42.040
and another button and they change color.

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:44.800
And a few buttons and a sequence happens.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:46.870
We were performing in public spaces

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:48.870
and the more positive reactions we got,

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:51.260
the more confident I
was to just go for it.

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:53.100
And just a few months after that,

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:54.390
we were on America's Got Talent,

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:56.490
and the rest it kind of history.

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:58.350
- It's ground-breaking what you do.

00:01:58.350 --> 00:01:59.610
It’s incredible. (crowd cheers)

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:04.610
you create everything from
zero and it's just brilliant.

00:02:05.028 --> 00:02:08.843
- We've worked with Chris
Brown, Death Cab for Cutie,

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:12.440
Christina Aguilera, Black Eyed Peas.

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:14.720
Then we also had our own show,

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:17.210
that has been in the heart
of Broadway for several years

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:20.130
and is touring both nationally
and internationally.

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:21.453
It can go on and on.

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:28.880
The future for iLuminate
is definitely education.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:31.210
I want to be able to have students

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:33.990
from different backgrounds
work and collaborate together,

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:36.480
because if you learn how to respect people

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:38.320
who do something different than you

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:40.540
and have them respect you back,

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:44.423
that kind of skillset will
really take you farther in life.

